    {
      "id": "claim_74c34f9ca50c44159059453f540d0be3",
      "statement": "Feature freeze is entered when the core loop completes once from both CLI and Web, key safety tests cover confirmation/daily limit/send windows/duplicate sends, install/configuration/stop/recovery are documented and reproducible, known P0/P1 defects are cleared with P2 defects dispositioned, and the release check is repeatable and stable; during freeze only serious bug fixes, security fixes, selector adaptations, and documentation updates are accepted.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/%E6%8A%80%E6%9C%AF%E6%89%8B%E5%86%8C.md#L565-L573",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:44a43e713b3be18563152b2cf1e6602be5014fc5c4f606669945c4788c8ac739:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_9a20e7b7a7f443febe68d6ee1df188bf",
      "statement": "Maintenance priority is ordered as security/privacy issues, then data corruption or duplicate sends, then core-flow unavailability, then platform selector adaptation, then observability and documentation, then experience polish, and new features last.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/%E6%8A%80%E6%9C%AF%E6%89%8B%E5%86%8C.md#L575-L580",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b65cff7e484431979d54a83846ce7fb218d2db40e872619c549195a34f5e6624:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d51f90006d924ab08afffe7223630ba3",
      "statement": "Work in progress is limited to one product feature at a time; a feature without completed tests and documentation blocks the next feature; new ideas go to Issue/Backlog rather than code; and experimental features with low usage and high maintenance cost for two consecutive versions are evaluated for deletion or freezing.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/%E6%8A%80%E6%9C%AF%E6%89%8B%E5%86%8C.md#L582-L587",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:03b9f4b52611693dc5bbdae92bd3c6b4e38449d0983319dd57b64c9ec27a24c0:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_0f38ac5f05a64f62b4e27a72cafdc644",
      "statement": "Development stops and re-enters review when a requirement changes product positioning or bypasses safety, one fix introduces multiple new services or long-term operational burden, acceptance criteria stay unclear while implementation is repeatedly adjusted, tests cannot stably reproduce the problem, or change benefit is smaller than account/privacy/compatibility/maintenance risk.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/%E6%8A%80%E6%9C%AF%E6%89%8B%E5%86%8C.md#L589-L597",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c3902ce83864e88dd2b6b615e7b605da93ee4df13c8d2c9928308113f5cf8710:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c5e4604a356a499dbfcbf2a6b4ceb56d",
      "statement": "New requirements must pass a five-question admission gate (loop improvement, real user problem, config/docs/existing-capability sufficiency, risk expansion, and clear acceptance/test/maintainer) and are default-rejected when they bypass confirmation/platform controls/captcha, raise default frequency or concurrency only to increase volume, add generic platform features, lack testable acceptance criteria, introduce long-term infrastructure cost without a use case, or duplicate existing capability.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/%E6%8A%80%E6%9C%AF%E6%89%8B%E5%86%8C.md#L522-L539",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1abff4ac5c758f2d0b94ecf1924267cc69a85ae7a0e1bbe5b15be9d6dbb75073:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_e2c25c6a3d7a4fcea0c2949feadc927a",
      "statement": "Accepted PR types are bug fixes, selector adaptations, documentation improvements, and new features discussed in an issue first; rejected PR types are those that raise the default send frequency, bypass human confirmation, add platform-safety-evasion methods, or reduce anti-detection conservatism such as shortening intervals or widening send windows.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://CONTRIBUTING.md#L18-L30",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9c7860db1d96dc2eddad01bf5db12662529a9fa77f7c1cb6251428955a7300df:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ab9ac2dd44414b0eb1f91cabf79256f6",
      "statement": "Failures are graded P0 through P3: P0 (key/resume leak, confirmation bypass, duplicate bulk send) requires stopping service, isolating data, revoking credentials, and fixing first; P1 (core flow unavailable, database corruption, wrong state risking mis-send) requires stopping the affected feature, preserving evidence, and releasing a regression-tested fix; P2 (single selector failure, partial AI-provider anomaly, PDF template problem) degrades or runs manually while a fix is scheduled; P3 (copy, styling, small UX) enters Backlog for a maintenance release; during any failure the database and browser config must not be deleted, and the response is stop, back up, record version and repro, then read-only diagnosis.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/%E6%8A%80%E6%9C%AF%E6%89%8B%E5%86%8C.md#L629-L638",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9ece8582a26e953e69028974dda731faa18032a52fffc0f1508bc9e1d1836455:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_271699abcf264cf782fa07ce876f7110",
      "statement": "Documentation ownership is split by surface: user command/operation changes update the operations manual and CLI help, architecture/state/config/release-process changes update the technical manual, product-intro changes update README, contribution-boundary changes update CONTRIBUTING, and security/interaction-behavior changes also review CLAUDE.md and SKILL.md; when docs and implementation conflict, the stricter safety boundary wins.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/%E6%8A%80%E6%9C%AF%E6%89%8B%E5%86%8C.md#L640-L648",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9583212c13c9b107ea3813860f22846f7d5040545797eb968f73f47a76ec4921:"
        }
      ]
    },
